-- title:
--   Cyclic Γ(q)-action of order dividing q+1 on the blow-up chart
-- statement:
--   Data and standing hypotheses. Let $q$ be a prime and $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q \nmid M'$ (`hqM'`), and let $\ell$ be a prime with $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ (`hℓ12`) and $\ell \mid M'$ (`hℓM'`). Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero and $\zeta \in L$ a primitive $q$-th root of unity (`hζ`), such that some ring homomorphism $\iota : L \to \mathbb C$ satisfies $\iota\zeta = \exp(2\pi i/q)$ (`hι`). Let $H_1 \le (\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ be, by `hH₁`, the intersection of [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.levelH q M'`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelJacobian.html#L22) — the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$ — with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/\ell)^\times$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ which, by `hK`, is [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.xHFunctionField (q ^ 2 * M') H₁)`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103): the subfield of $L((t))$ generated over $L$ by the coefficientwise image, under $\mathbb Q \to L$, of the $q$-expansion function field of $X_{H_1}$ of level $q^2M'$.
--
--   Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with $\mathrm{Frac}\,A = L$ (via the given algebra structure and `IsFractionRing`), henselian and with algebraically closed residue field, with $q \in \mathfrak m_A$ (`hAq`) and with $\zeta$ in the image of $A$ (`hζA`), equipped with an algebra structure on $K$ compatible with that on $L$. Let $j \in K$ be nonzero whose image in $L((t))$ is the $j$-series [`ModularCurve.coeffEmb L ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L81) (`hj`). Let $\varpi$ generate $\mathfrak m_A$ (`hϖ`), and let $\varpi_t \in A$ satisfy $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   Write $C =$ `chartAlgFin A (↥K) j` for the finite chart algebra, i.e. the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ of elements integral over $A[j]$, with distinguished element `jChartFin A (↥K) j` $= j$; and let $X =$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel A (↥K) j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L236) be the two-chart integral model, the pushout of $\operatorname{Spec} C$ and $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the corresponding chart algebra of $j^{-1}$ along the middle chart, with structure morphism `toBase` to $\operatorname{Spec} A$ and closed-chart morphism `ιFin` from `XFin` $= \operatorname{Spec} C$.
--
--   Let $y \subset C$ be a maximal ideal (`hy`) containing $\varpi$ (`hϖy`) and supersingular in the sense of `hss`: for every algebraically closed field $\Omega$ of characteristic $q$ and every ring homomorphism $\varphi : C \to \Omega$ with kernel $y$, the element $\varphi(j)$ lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet q Ω`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7), the set of those $\bar j \in \Omega$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $\bar j$ has no nonzero affine point annihilated by $q$.
--
--   Throughout, for $\gamma \in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ the phrase "$\tau$ is a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$" abbreviates [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.IsLevelAutAt L q ζ q (q ^ 2 * M') H₁ γ⁻¹ K τ`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelLevelAutAt.html#L29), for an $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$: for every weight $k$, every pair $f,g$ of weight-$k$ modular forms for [`CohCarrier.GammaH (q ^ 2 * M') H₁`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133) (the image in $SL_2(\mathbb Z)$, read inside $GL_2(\mathbb R)$, of the preimage of $H_1$ under $\Gamma_0(q^2M') \to (\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$) with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$, $p_g$ having nonzero image, and every $x \in K$ whose Laurent series is the coefficient embedding of $p_f/p_g$, the coefficientwise image of $\tau x$ under any $\iota : L \to \mathbb C$ with $\iota\zeta = \exp(2\pi i/q)$ satisfies $\iota(\tau x)\cdot (g\mid_k \sigma)^\wedge = (f\mid_k \sigma)^\wedge$ on $q$-expansions, where $\sigma =$ `conjElemN q γ⁻¹`.
--
--   The rigidification hypothesis `hArig` (summarised here) requires the following at every relevant point: for every $z \in X$ such that the germ $\varpi_z$ at $z$ of the pullback of $\varpi$ along `toBase` lies in the maximal ideal of the stalk $\mathcal O_{X,z}$, and every point $y'$ of `XFin` with `ιFin`$(y') = z$ whose ideal is supersingular in the sense of `hss` above, there exist a complete discrete valuation domain $W$, a ring homomorphism $\sigma : A \to W$ with $\mathfrak m_W = (\sigma\varpi)$, power series $f,u,v \in W[[X_0,X_1]]$ with $u,v$ units and $f - (X_0X_1^q - X_0^qX_1) \in (X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$ (the Drinfeld form [`DrinfeldCurve.LocalChart.drinfeldForm q W`](def/DrinfeldCurve_LocalChart.html#L18)), and a ring isomorphism $e$ from the adic completion of $\mathcal O_{X,z}$ onto $S = W[[X_0,X_1]]/(\sigma(\varpi_t^{\,q+1})v - fu)$, such that, writing `toC` for the map from the stalk to its completion, `mkS` for the quotient map and `germY` for the germ map $C \to \mathcal O_{X,z}$ through the chart $y'$: (i) $e$ carries the image of $a \in A$ to the constant $\sigma a$; (ii) every level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ maps $C$ into $C$; (iii) if moreover $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \bmod \ell$, the induced endomorphism of $C$ is congruent to the identity modulo $y'$; (iv) for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $C$ and congruent to the identity modulo $y'$, there are a ring automorphism $\theta$ of $S$, a scalar $c \in W$ and a matrix $M \in M_2(W)$ with $\theta$ compatible with $\tau$ via $e \circ$ `toC` $\circ$ `germY`, $\theta$ fixing all constants, $\theta(X_{j}) \equiv \sum_i M_{ij}X_i$ modulo the square of the ideal generated by the images of $X_0,X_1$, $c^{q+1} \equiv 1$ and $M \equiv c\gamma$ entrywise modulo $\mathfrak m_W$, together with $c \equiv 1 \bmod \mathfrak m_W$ whenever $\gamma_{11} \equiv 1 \bmod \ell$, and $c \not\equiv 1 \bmod \mathfrak m_W$ whenever $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; (v) two primes $P_1,P_2$ of $S$, each omitting one of the images of $X_0,X_1$, each containing $\sigma\varpi$ and each containing an element $a_iX_0 + b_iX_1 + (\text{terms in } (X_0,X_1)^2)$ with $q \nmid a_1b_2 - a_2b_1$, have distinct contractions to the stalk; (vi) for a prime $P$ of $S$ of this shape with $(a,b) = (1,0)$, an element of $C$ has germ in the contraction of $P$ exactly when all its Laurent coefficients lie in $\mathfrak m_A$; (vii) [`ModularCurve.jqNModC L q`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L18) lies in $K$ and in $C$, and there are $a_0 \in A$ with `jqNModC L q` $- a_0 \in y'$, an integer $e_0 \ge 1$ and $h \in (X_0,X_1)^{e_0}$ whose degree-$e_0$ binary form $\sum_{i\le e_0} (\text{coeff}_{X_0^iX_1^{e_0-i}}h)\,a^ib^{e_0-i}$ is a unit for all $a,b \in W$ not both in $\mathfrak m_W$ with $a^qb - ab^q \in \mathfrak m_W$, and such that the image of the germ of `jqNModC L q` $- a_0$ in $S$ is $h$.
--
--   A single point and a single presentation are then fixed: a point $z \in X$ with $\varpi_z$ in the maximal ideal of the stalk (`hϖz`, `hz`), a point $y'$ of `XFin` over $z$ (`hy'`) which is supersingular (`hss'`) and whose ideal equals $y$ (`hy'y`); and data $W_1, \sigma_1, f_1, u_1, v_1, e_1$ of exactly the shape above (with $\mathfrak m_{W_1} = (\sigma_1\varpi)$, $u_1,v_1$ units, $f_1$ congruent to the Drinfeld form modulo $(X_0,X_1)^{q+2}$, and $e_1$ an isomorphism from the completed stalk at $z$ onto $S = W_1[[X_0,X_1]]/(\sigma_1(\varpi_t^{\,q+1})v_1 - f_1u_1)$), subject to the hypothesis `hW₁`, which asserts for this presentation the same seven clauses (i)–(vii) listed above, with $W,\sigma,e$ replaced by $W_1,\sigma_1,e_1$.
--
--   Blow-up data. Let $J \subseteq C$ be an ideal which, by `hJ`, is the infimum of the set of ideals $J'$ of $C$ of the form $J' =$ the preimage, under the restriction of a level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ to $C$, of the contraction along $e_1 \circ$ `toC` $\circ$ `germY` of the ideal of $S$ generated by the images of $\sigma_1\varpi_t$, $X_0$ and $X_1$, the infimum being over all $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and all such $\tau$ preserving $C$. Let $B$ be the $A$-subalgebra of $K$ which, by `hB`, is generated over $C$ by $\{x \in K : x\varpi_t \in J\}$, that is the blow-up chart $C[J/\varpi_t]$. Let $\mathcal W$ be a valuation subring of $K$ containing $B$ (`hBW`).
--
--   The hypotheses on this data are: `hR1`, that $C \subseteq B$ and every element of $K$ is a ratio $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$, $h \ne 0$; `hR2`, that $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A$ and that $B/\varpi B$ has Krull dimension at most $1$; `hR3` (five clauses), that an element of $L$ lies in $\mathcal W$ exactly when it comes from $A$, that $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal W}$ is generated by $\varpi$, that $\mathcal W$ is a discrete valuation ring, that an element of $C$ lies in $y$ exactly when it lies in $\mathcal W$ and in $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal W}$, and that $\mathcal W$ is the set of ratios $g/h$ with $g,h \in B$ and $h \notin \mathfrak m_{\mathcal W}$; and `hEQ` (five clauses, summarised here), that for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on the residue field $k$ of $A$ there is a surjective ring homomorphism $\rho : B \to$ [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q k`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) $= k[x_0,x_1]/(\mathrm{drinfeldPoly} - 1)$ whose kernel consists of the elements of $B$ lying in $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal W}$, which is compatible with $A \to k$, and which is equivariant for level automorphisms in the sense that for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ and $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ preserving $\mathcal W$ there is $c \in \mathbb F_{q^2}^\times$ with $(\mathrm{redQ}\,\gamma, c)$ in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276) (the kernel of the character $(g,c) \mapsto \det g \cdot c^{q+1}$) such that $\rho \circ \tau =$ `hAction` of that element applied to $\rho$, with $c \ne 1$ when $\gamma \in \Gamma(q)$ and $\tau \ne \mathrm{id}$; that $B$ is stable under all level automorphisms at $\gamma^{-1}$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$; that every prime $Q$ of $B$ containing $\varpi$ is obtained by transporting the centre $\{b : b \in \mathfrak m_{\mathcal W}\}$ into $Q$ by some level automorphism attached to some $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$; that an element of $B$ all of whose translates under such automorphisms lie in $\mathfrak m_{\mathcal W}$ is divisible by $\varpi$; and that a level automorphism at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ preserves $\mathcal W$ as soon as it preserves $y$ on $C$.
--
--   Conclusion. There exist a natural number $n$ with $1 \le n$ and $n \mid q+1$, a matrix $\gamma_0 \in SL_2(\mathbb Z)$ lying both in $\Gamma(q)$ and in $\Gamma_0(M')$, and an $L$-algebra automorphism $\tau_0$ of $K$ which is a level automorphism at $\gamma_0^{-1}$ and satisfies $f \in \mathcal W \iff \tau_0 f \in \mathcal W$ for all $f \in K$, such that:
--
--   (1) $\tau_0^{\,n}$ fixes every element of $B$;
--
--   (2) for every $k$ with $0 < k < n$ there is $f \in B$ with $\tau_0^{\,k} f \ne f$;
--
--   (3) for every $\gamma \in \Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ and every level automorphism $\tau$ at $\gamma^{-1}$ with $f \in \mathcal W \iff \tau f \in \mathcal W$, there is $k < n$ with $\tau f = \tau_0^{\,k} f$ for all $f \in B$.
--
--   Thus the level automorphisms coming from $\Gamma(q) \cap \Gamma_0(M')$ which preserve the valuation ring $\mathcal W$ act on the blow-up chart $B$ through a cyclic group of order $n \mid q+1$ generated by $\tau_0|_B$.
--
--   This is the statement that the decomposition group at an end of the blown-up supersingular chart acts on that chart through a cyclic group of order dividing $q+1$: the $\Gamma(q)$-part of the stabiliser of the valuation $\mathcal W$ restricts to $B$ as the cyclic group generated by one automorphism $\tau_0$. It is the auxiliary-level variant in which the auxiliary full level is replaced by a diamond condition at a guard prime $\ell \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ dividing $M'$, and it feeds the assembly of the cyclic decomposition of the ends of the supersingular fibre, where the Drinfeld-chart and Hasse data of the hypotheses are combined with the Igusa separation statements.
